<manifest>
  <!--
    Intentionally empty.

    The receiver behind the Picture-in-Picture actions is registered at RUNTIME
    (`ContextCompat.registerReceiver(..., RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED)`) for exactly as
    long as JS is listening, so it needs no manifest entry — and declaring one
    would publish a component that outlives the session and is reachable by the
    whole system rather than only by our own PendingIntents.

    `android:supportsPictureInPicture` on the main activity is the expo-video
    config plugin's job (see the `expo-video` entry in `app.config.js`); this
    module only adds actions to a window that plugin already made possible.
  -->
</manifest>
